@startuml physical-view-airports-routes-mode-a
skinparam shadowing false
title Airports & Routes - physical view (Mode A: IntelliJ + infrastructure in Docker)

node "Developer PC (Windows)" {
  node "start-infra.ps1" {
    node "NGINX gateway\nhttps://localhost:8443" as GW
    node "Keycloak\nhttp://localhost:8180" as KC
  }
  node "IntelliJ (Spring Boot run configurations)" {
    node "Airports - Instância 1\n:8091 (profile inst1)" as AR1
    node "Airports - Instância 2\n:8092 (profile inst2)" as AR2
    node "Airports - Instância 3\n:8093 (profile inst3)" as AR3
    node "FlightOperations 1/2/3\n:8081-8083" as FO
  }
  database "H2 file\ndata/airports_db_1" as H1
  database "H2 file\ndata/airports_db_2" as H2
  database "H2 file\ndata/airports_db_3" as H3
  node "Docker Desktop" {
    node "RabbitMQ (single node)\nAMQP :5672, UI :15672\n(docker-compose.services.yml)" as MQ
    database "fo-db-a1/a2/a3\nPostgreSQL :5441-5443" as FODB
  }
}

actor "Client / Postman" as C
C --> GW : HTTPS
C --> AR1 : HTTPS (direct access\nfor tests)
GW --> AR1
GW --> AR2
GW --> AR3
GW --> KC
AR1 --> H1 : JDBC
AR2 --> H2 : JDBC
AR3 --> H3 : JDBC
AR1 --> MQ : AMQP
AR2 --> MQ : AMQP
AR3 --> MQ : AMQP
FO --> MQ : AMQP (fo.routes.fo-N)
FO --> FODB : JDBC

note bottom of H2
  Database-per-instance also in Mode A: each instance has
  its own H2 file (write + read model, outbox, inbox),
  created by the same Flyway migrations as in Mode B.
  Queues: airports.events.<port> (quorum), one per instance.
end note
note right of MQ
  Single node: no broker redundancy in Mode A
  (development). The 3-node cluster and PostgreSQL
  per instance are in Mode B.
end note
@enduml
